1
00:00:01,106 --> 00:00:04,026
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,111
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,646 --> 00:00:44,066
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:46,902
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:49,071
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,157 --> 00:00:54,534
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

7
00:01:05,754 --> 00:01:06,797
[blade swooshing]

8
00:01:07,714 --> 00:01:08,924
[♪ music swells]

9
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,138
[Gaeun panting]

10
00:01:16,264 --> 00:01:17,557
[panting, breath trembling]

11
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:20,102
-[stick taps twice]
-What are you doing?

12
00:01:20,185 --> 00:01:21,937
[Gaeun, breath trembling]

13
00:01:22,646 --> 00:01:24,856
Gaeun, what's wrong?

14
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:26,817
[breathing heavily]

15
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,694
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

16
00:01:31,363 --> 00:01:32,614
I'm the lead dancer.

17
00:01:34,658 --> 00:01:36,410
I'm the lead dancer.

18
00:01:38,787 --> 00:01:40,706
-[barks]
-[K9 handler] Shush. [mutters]

19
00:01:46,128 --> 00:01:47,504
SONG GAEUN

20
00:01:49,631 --> 00:01:52,050
I'm the lead dancer. [gasping shakily]

21
00:01:52,134 --> 00:01:53,301
[Dahye] Hey...

22
00:01:54,845 --> 00:01:56,304
[♪ music swells]

23
00:02:02,185 --> 00:02:03,645
-[sharp swoosh, slash]
-[shrieks, echoing]

24
00:02:03,728 --> 00:02:04,729
[♪ music fades]

25
00:02:05,439 --> 00:02:07,399
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

26
00:02:09,818 --> 00:02:11,778
[Gaeun gasping shakily]

27
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:15,365
[breathing heavily]

28
00:02:20,996 --> 00:02:22,539
[♪ music increases in tempo]

29
00:02:22,622 --> 00:02:24,166
[panting, gasping]

30
00:02:31,423 --> 00:02:32,549
[sword clatters]

31
00:02:33,717 --> 00:02:34,968
[gasping]

32
00:02:35,051 --> 00:02:37,137
[panting, gasping]

33
00:02:40,182 --> 00:02:41,808
[♪ music swells]

34
00:02:44,895 --> 00:02:46,271
[Gaeun continues panting]

35
00:02:48,023 --> 00:02:49,274
[♪ music fades]

36
00:02:50,233 --> 00:02:51,860
[siren blaring]

37
00:02:51,943 --> 00:02:53,528
[students whispering anxiously]

38
00:02:59,659 --> 00:03:01,578
EPISODE 10

39
00:03:02,954 --> 00:03:04,915
Is the culprit among them?

40
00:03:05,624 --> 00:03:07,167
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

41
00:03:10,962 --> 00:03:12,214
How did it go?

42
00:03:12,297 --> 00:03:14,049
We found some traces here and there.

43
00:03:14,132 --> 00:03:16,176
But we can't narrow down a suspect.

44
00:03:16,259 --> 00:03:18,345
Too many people use this space.

45
00:03:19,513 --> 00:03:21,097
-Okay. Thank you for coming.
-[K9 handler] Sure.

46
00:03:25,519 --> 00:03:26,645
What happened?

47
00:03:27,521 --> 00:03:30,190
A curse pouch was found in Seyeon's bag,

48
00:03:30,273 --> 00:03:31,316
and it had drugs inside.

49
00:03:32,025 --> 00:03:33,026
Drugs?

50
00:03:33,109 --> 00:03:35,445
Gaeun was hallucinating
because of the same drug.

51
00:03:40,242 --> 00:03:43,537
Are you saying one of my students
did something like that?

52
00:03:45,997 --> 00:03:48,041
Don't tell the students anything just yet.

53
00:03:57,551 --> 00:03:58,677
[♪ music fades]

54
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:01,054
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

55
00:04:01,137 --> 00:04:03,098
[Junyoung] This is
commonly known as "Ruby."

56
00:04:03,181 --> 00:04:05,475
Just touching it can make you hallucinate.

57
00:04:05,559 --> 00:04:08,853
It's sold anonymously on the dark web,
so they can't identify the buyers.

58
00:04:08,937 --> 00:04:10,230
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

59
00:04:10,313 --> 00:04:11,481
CONTACT WITH NARCOTIC SUBSTANCE

60
00:04:11,565 --> 00:04:13,024
HALLUCINATION
REPEATEDLY STRUCK LEGS

61
00:04:13,108 --> 00:04:16,987
So Seyeon touched those rubies
and died from an asthma attack?

62
00:04:17,070 --> 00:04:18,321
Yes.

63
00:04:18,405 --> 00:04:20,824
They may not have intended it,
but it ended in a murder.

64
00:04:20,907 --> 00:04:22,576
But even so,

65
00:04:22,659 --> 00:04:25,662
could a high school student get
their hands on a drug like this?

66
00:04:25,745 --> 00:04:28,415
It's not impossible.
The dark web doesn't have an age limit.

67
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,292
[Isoo] I don't understand

68
00:04:30,375 --> 00:04:32,419
cursing someone
just to steal the lead role.

69
00:04:32,502 --> 00:04:34,671
I heard the arts festival
is a pretty big deal.

70
00:04:35,297 --> 00:04:37,340
All the famous
dance companies will be there.

71
00:04:37,966 --> 00:04:39,759
We can't trace the drug,

72
00:04:40,635 --> 00:04:42,387
so we'll have to go after the curse pouch.

73
00:04:42,470 --> 00:04:44,139
Check the footage from the Witch's Shop.

74
00:04:44,222 --> 00:04:46,433
Make a list of everyone
who bought a curse pouch.

75
00:04:46,516 --> 00:04:47,809
Got it.

76
00:04:47,893 --> 00:04:49,728
[♪ music increases in tempo]

77
00:04:56,818 --> 00:04:57,903
[keyboard clacks]

78
00:04:59,112 --> 00:05:00,113
Detective Joo.

79
00:05:01,031 --> 00:05:02,824
A student bought one
the day before the incident.

80
00:05:06,703 --> 00:05:08,538
[♪ music swells]

81
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:12,792
[♪ music resumes tempo]

82
00:05:12,876 --> 00:05:14,044
That's Hayun.

83
00:05:18,214 --> 00:05:19,299
[♪ music fades]

84
00:05:23,511 --> 00:05:24,512
Hi, Hayun.

85
00:05:27,724 --> 00:05:29,392
Can we talk for a moment?

86
00:05:31,269 --> 00:05:32,437
[Isoo] Hayun, what will you have?

87
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:33,897
I'm fine.

88
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:35,941
You should eat something.

89
00:05:37,817 --> 00:05:39,694
Then I'll get the Chicken Bacon Mini Wrap.

90
00:05:39,778 --> 00:05:42,364
Okay. Italian B.M.T. for you,
Detective Joo?

91
00:05:42,447 --> 00:05:43,698
Yeah. Coffee, too.

92
00:05:43,782 --> 00:05:45,408
Coffee? What about you, Hayun?

93
00:05:46,409 --> 00:05:47,452
I'll just drink water.

94
00:05:47,535 --> 00:05:49,746
No. Jin Isoo is buying today.

95
00:05:50,664 --> 00:05:51,915
Want anything more to eat, huh?

96
00:05:54,042 --> 00:05:56,336
You must be startled
after what happened with Gaeun.

97
00:05:56,419 --> 00:05:58,505
Yeah, why did she do that?

98
00:05:59,005 --> 00:06:00,006
I'm not sure.

99
00:06:01,341 --> 00:06:03,802
Have your friends said anything about it?

100
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:07,263
They said maybe she lost it
after getting the lead.

101
00:06:07,347 --> 00:06:08,556
Ah. [chuckles softly]

102
00:06:13,061 --> 00:06:14,104
[Isoo] Mmm.

103
00:06:14,854 --> 00:06:16,356
[♪ jaunty, dramatic music playing]

104
00:06:18,316 --> 00:06:19,317
All right.

105
00:06:20,986 --> 00:06:22,946
Here, drink this.

106
00:06:23,029 --> 00:06:24,447
Coffee for Detective Joo.

107
00:06:24,990 --> 00:06:25,991
Let's eat.

108
00:06:26,616 --> 00:06:27,742
[softly] Mmm...

109
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:31,204
Mmm!

110
00:06:34,916 --> 00:06:36,167
Mmm!

111
00:06:36,251 --> 00:06:37,252
It's good, right?

112
00:06:37,335 --> 00:06:38,795
-Right?
-Yes.

113
00:06:38,878 --> 00:06:40,755
You girls are always on a diet, huh.

114
00:06:40,839 --> 00:06:42,507
You need to eat well for your arm to heal.

115
00:06:47,721 --> 00:06:49,347
Can you pick that up for me?

116
00:06:52,642 --> 00:06:53,685
[♪ music fades]

117
00:06:58,148 --> 00:06:59,149
You're right.

118
00:07:00,066 --> 00:07:01,985
I put this inside Seyeon's bag.

119
00:07:03,111 --> 00:07:04,112
Gaeun, too?

120
00:07:05,447 --> 00:07:08,366
Gaeun? What about Gaeun?

121
00:07:11,411 --> 00:07:12,829
But how did you know?

122
00:07:13,455 --> 00:07:14,664
Mmm.

123
00:07:15,206 --> 00:07:16,291
The security camera.

124
00:07:17,917 --> 00:07:19,419
[chuckles nervously, swears softly]

125
00:07:20,628 --> 00:07:21,713
So, what about it?

126
00:07:22,547 --> 00:07:24,632
[wrapper crumpling]

127
00:07:25,592 --> 00:07:27,635
Seyeon died because of that pouch.

128
00:07:30,472 --> 00:07:32,182
Is this a real curse?

129
00:07:33,224 --> 00:07:34,809
I was only messing around.

130
00:07:34,893 --> 00:07:35,894
No.

131
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:39,314
There was a drug inside
that causes hallucinations.

132
00:07:39,397 --> 00:07:40,398
What?

133
00:07:40,482 --> 00:07:41,566
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

134
00:07:41,649 --> 00:07:43,026
What are you talking about?

135
00:07:43,902 --> 00:07:45,320
Uh, if, by any chance,

136
00:07:46,112 --> 00:07:47,238
you put it in as a joke--

137
00:07:47,322 --> 00:07:49,491
What are you talking about?
Do you think I'm crazy?

138
00:07:52,452 --> 00:07:54,120
It really wasn't me.

139
00:07:54,204 --> 00:07:56,790
I did it because I was annoyed.
Where would I even get drugs?

140
00:07:58,249 --> 00:07:59,918
If I got caught, I'd be expelled.

141
00:08:01,044 --> 00:08:02,796
And everyone at school does this.

142
00:08:02,879 --> 00:08:04,756
They send curses
to people they don't like.

143
00:08:04,839 --> 00:08:06,257
The principal knows as well.

144
00:08:06,341 --> 00:08:07,884
Some kids had theirs confiscated.

145
00:08:08,468 --> 00:08:09,677
The principal knows, too?

146
00:08:09,761 --> 00:08:11,429
Yes. Go ask her.

147
00:08:13,056 --> 00:08:14,641
When did you put the pouch in?

148
00:08:18,812 --> 00:08:21,856
During the afternoon class
on the day Seyeon died.

149
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:23,942
CHANGING ROOM

150
00:08:29,364 --> 00:08:30,949
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

151
00:08:48,716 --> 00:08:50,176
MOON SEYEON

152
00:08:57,851 --> 00:09:00,186
I got really scared
when she actually died.

153
00:09:04,315 --> 00:09:05,316
[♪ music fades]

154
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,861
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

155
00:09:07,944 --> 00:09:08,945
KIM HAYUN

156
00:09:09,028 --> 00:09:11,447
I don't think Hayun is the culprit.

157
00:09:12,157 --> 00:09:13,408
Detective Choi.

158
00:09:13,491 --> 00:09:15,994
Let's see the hallway
outside the studio that afternoon.

159
00:09:16,077 --> 00:09:17,078
Okay.

160
00:09:17,162 --> 00:09:18,997
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

161
00:09:39,559 --> 00:09:41,978
Did Hayun just put the pouch in?

162
00:10:08,213 --> 00:10:09,505
-Wait.
-[keyboard clacks]

163
00:10:10,131 --> 00:10:11,382
What's this?

164
00:10:11,466 --> 00:10:13,092
[Junyoung] Principal Jeong Joohee?

165
00:10:14,719 --> 00:10:16,638
The principal slipped in the drugs?

166
00:10:18,264 --> 00:10:19,891
The principal killed Seyeon?

167
00:10:19,974 --> 00:10:21,935
She has no reason to.

168
00:10:22,685 --> 00:10:24,812
She said she gave Seyeon
the lead because of her asthma.

169
00:10:25,438 --> 00:10:27,315
She might've gone in to get something.

170
00:10:27,398 --> 00:10:30,443
Anyone could have gotten to Seyeon's bag.

171
00:10:31,152 --> 00:10:33,863
If all those students
are giving each other curses,

172
00:10:33,947 --> 00:10:35,698
how can we narrow down the suspects?

173
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:38,201
[sighs softly]

174
00:10:40,119 --> 00:10:41,955
Did you find anything on Seyeon's phone?

175
00:10:43,581 --> 00:10:44,624
Nothing significant.

176
00:10:47,627 --> 00:10:48,711
[sighs softly]

177
00:10:48,795 --> 00:10:50,380
I CURSE YOU, MOON SEYEON
DIE, DIE!

178
00:10:50,463 --> 00:10:51,714
By the way,

179
00:10:52,507 --> 00:10:54,968
if she wanted to curse someone,
why not write their name?

180
00:10:55,051 --> 00:10:56,970
Why just write that she cursed them?

181
00:10:57,053 --> 00:10:59,681
Maybe she wanted to curse multiple people.

182
00:10:59,764 --> 00:11:01,766
Like the ones responsible for her death.

183
00:11:01,849 --> 00:11:04,727
But there wasn't anyone like that.

184
00:11:04,811 --> 00:11:06,271
[♪ music swells]

185
00:11:10,275 --> 00:11:12,026
[♪ music fades]

186
00:11:12,110 --> 00:11:13,111
Huh?

187
00:11:15,154 --> 00:11:16,531
[♪ suspenseful music plays, swells]

188
00:11:16,614 --> 00:11:18,616
I CURSE YOU

189
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:20,159
[in English] What the...
[in Korean] Oh, my God!

190
00:11:20,243 --> 00:11:21,577
[♪ music fades]

191
00:11:21,661 --> 00:11:23,496
Hey, come here.

192
00:11:23,579 --> 00:11:26,124
-What is it?
-I think I'm a freaking genius.

193
00:11:26,207 --> 00:11:27,458
Look.

194
00:11:27,542 --> 00:11:29,585
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

195
00:11:36,050 --> 00:11:37,802
JEONG JOOHEE

196
00:11:37,885 --> 00:11:38,970
[gasps]

197
00:11:40,596 --> 00:11:42,473
"Jeong Joohee"?

198
00:11:46,311 --> 00:11:49,230
Maybe what Yuna actually wanted
to write was "Jeong Joohee."

199
00:11:50,315 --> 00:11:54,235
Jeong Joohee was the one
who killed Baek Yuna?

200
00:11:56,904 --> 00:11:57,905
She made her kill herself?

201
00:11:58,656 --> 00:11:59,741
But why?

202
00:12:00,408 --> 00:12:02,702
She even received money
from Baek Yuna's parents.

203
00:12:03,703 --> 00:12:06,080
Jeong Joohee is suspicious, though.

204
00:12:07,081 --> 00:12:10,626
Right. She knew about the curse pouch,
but pretended not to.

205
00:12:14,630 --> 00:12:15,631
What's this?

206
00:12:16,966 --> 00:12:18,343
Have you never seen it before?

207
00:12:18,426 --> 00:12:20,595
It's a trend among the students.

208
00:12:20,678 --> 00:12:22,055
It's a curse pouch.

209
00:12:22,847 --> 00:12:24,974
The students carry this around?

210
00:12:28,644 --> 00:12:30,021
Gaeun also said something, too.

211
00:12:30,104 --> 00:12:31,689
But Seyeon told me

212
00:12:32,565 --> 00:12:35,193
the principal has no choice
but to pick her for the lead.

213
00:12:39,655 --> 00:12:41,783
Seyeon didn't have the money to bribe her,

214
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:46,788
so why did Jeong Joohee have
no choice but to pick her as the lead?

215
00:12:46,871 --> 00:12:48,206
[♪ music swells]

216
00:12:54,504 --> 00:12:57,548
JEONG JOOHEE

217
00:12:57,632 --> 00:12:58,674
[♪ music fades]

218
00:12:59,884 --> 00:13:01,260
[Isoo] Ma'am,

219
00:13:01,344 --> 00:13:05,014
it seems the principal
was very fond of Seyeon.

220
00:13:05,890 --> 00:13:07,308
She was.

221
00:13:07,392 --> 00:13:09,018
She came to see me.

222
00:13:09,102 --> 00:13:11,854
Principal Jeong Joohee came to see you?

223
00:13:11,938 --> 00:13:12,980
[Grandma] Yes.

224
00:13:13,564 --> 00:13:14,649
She said she felt bad.

225
00:13:14,732 --> 00:13:16,025
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

226
00:13:16,109 --> 00:13:17,860
She brought that with her.

227
00:13:19,737 --> 00:13:23,825
Thank you for coming all the way
to this humble place, Principal Jeong.

228
00:13:24,826 --> 00:13:26,702
You must be heartbroken.

229
00:13:27,412 --> 00:13:32,917
<i>But she said</i>
<i>she had left something with Seyeon.</i>

230
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,836
[drawer opens, rummaging]

231
00:13:36,254 --> 00:13:37,255
[drawer closes]

232
00:13:37,338 --> 00:13:38,339
[drawer opens]

233
00:13:38,423 --> 00:13:39,966
[♪ music increases in tempo]

234
00:13:40,716 --> 00:13:41,968
[rummaging continues]

235
00:13:42,051 --> 00:13:44,262
She searched Seyeon's room?

236
00:13:44,345 --> 00:13:45,346
[Grandma] Yes.

237
00:13:45,429 --> 00:13:48,516
But I don't think she found it.

238
00:13:48,599 --> 00:13:49,976
She just left.

239
00:13:50,059 --> 00:13:51,394
[♪ music resumes tempo]

240
00:13:52,061 --> 00:13:54,230
And you have no idea what it was?

241
00:13:54,313 --> 00:13:56,232
No, I wouldn't know.

242
00:13:57,984 --> 00:13:59,026
[♪ music fades]

243
00:13:59,110 --> 00:14:00,153
Ma'am.

244
00:14:01,195 --> 00:14:03,531
[exhales softly]
I figured you wouldn't have eaten.

245
00:14:04,991 --> 00:14:05,992
[♪ melancholy music playing]

246
00:14:06,075 --> 00:14:08,286
I don't know
if it's worth living like this.

247
00:14:10,288 --> 00:14:11,497
I outlived my daughter,

248
00:14:13,457 --> 00:14:15,376
and now I even lost

249
00:14:16,127 --> 00:14:18,004
my poor granddaughter. [sobbing]

250
00:14:25,303 --> 00:14:26,429
[♪ music fades]

251
00:14:26,512 --> 00:14:27,680
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

252
00:14:27,763 --> 00:14:29,765
[shaman] <i>An item with fur, about this big.</i>

253
00:14:30,474 --> 00:14:32,018
<i>She left it behind.</i>

254
00:14:32,101 --> 00:14:33,269
Ma'am.

255
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:38,566
Is this your phone?

256
00:14:38,649 --> 00:14:39,817
What's the matter?

257
00:14:39,901 --> 00:14:41,694
The shaman said she saw this.

258
00:14:43,738 --> 00:14:45,239
It used to be Seyeon's phone.

259
00:14:46,199 --> 00:14:48,326
She gave it to me a few months ago.

260
00:14:49,952 --> 00:14:51,287
May I take a look?

261
00:14:51,370 --> 00:14:52,914
Of course.

262
00:14:52,997 --> 00:14:54,123
-Feel free to.
-Okay.

263
00:14:54,207 --> 00:14:55,583
[♪ music increases in tempo]

264
00:15:01,088 --> 00:15:02,590
This is a video app.

265
00:15:04,383 --> 00:15:05,927
Ma'am, do you know what this is?

266
00:15:06,010 --> 00:15:07,887
I don't know any of that stuff.

267
00:15:07,970 --> 00:15:10,264
Ah. I'm going to take a look.

268
00:15:10,348 --> 00:15:11,682
-[Grandma] Okay.
-Thanks.

269
00:15:11,766 --> 00:15:13,226
-[♪ music swells]
-[Isoo inhales sharply]

270
00:15:16,145 --> 00:15:17,772
ALL VIDEOS

271
00:15:17,855 --> 00:15:19,732
[♪ music slows, turns ominous]

272
00:15:26,739 --> 00:15:28,115
[♪ music swells]

273
00:15:30,368 --> 00:15:32,078
[♪ music resumes tempo]

274
00:15:32,912 --> 00:15:33,996
[phone case snaps shut]

275
00:15:36,624 --> 00:15:37,625
Ma'am.

276
00:15:38,918 --> 00:15:40,628
Make sure you eat properly.

277
00:15:40,711 --> 00:15:42,672
Please stay healthy.

278
00:15:42,755 --> 00:15:46,175
We promise to catch the culprit
who did this to Seyeon.

279
00:15:47,301 --> 00:15:48,511
Thank you.

280
00:15:53,391 --> 00:15:54,475
[♪ music fades]

281
00:16:00,022 --> 00:16:01,691
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

282
00:16:04,735 --> 00:16:06,737
2025 JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL

283
00:16:06,821 --> 00:16:08,114
[indistinct chatter]

284
00:16:08,197 --> 00:16:09,991
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

285
00:16:43,149 --> 00:16:44,317
[spectral exhale]

286
00:16:45,192 --> 00:16:46,360
[spectral exhale]

287
00:16:46,444 --> 00:16:47,528
[♪ music swells]

288
00:16:49,196 --> 00:16:50,281
[♪ music fades]

289
00:16:50,364 --> 00:16:52,366
2025 JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL

290
00:16:52,450 --> 00:16:53,743
[indistinct chatter]

291
00:16:56,662 --> 00:16:58,414
2025 JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL

292
00:17:01,584 --> 00:17:03,336
[Isoo] No more cursing each other.

293
00:17:03,419 --> 00:17:06,839
You should all be
sharing good luck instead, okay?

294
00:17:06,922 --> 00:17:08,549
-[students] Okay.
-[Isoo] Here.

295
00:17:09,091 --> 00:17:10,134
[in English] Good luck.

296
00:17:10,634 --> 00:17:11,719
[in Korean] Here you go.

297
00:17:12,845 --> 00:17:14,096
Here you go.

298
00:17:15,473 --> 00:17:17,433
We came to see the performance, too.

299
00:17:17,892 --> 00:17:18,893
Sure.

300
00:17:18,976 --> 00:17:20,227
I hope you enjoy the show.

301
00:17:20,311 --> 00:17:22,438
Yes, I'm sure it'll be very enjoyable.

302
00:17:24,607 --> 00:17:25,900
All right, you got this!

303
00:17:25,983 --> 00:17:27,276
-We got this!
-We got this!

304
00:17:28,569 --> 00:17:30,196
Everyone ready?

305
00:17:30,279 --> 00:17:31,364
-Yes.
-Yes.

306
00:17:31,447 --> 00:17:33,366
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

307
00:17:36,327 --> 00:17:37,328
[door closes]

308
00:17:37,411 --> 00:17:38,704
[AV technician] Who are you?

309
00:17:40,039 --> 00:17:41,082
Excuse me for a moment.

310
00:17:41,707 --> 00:17:43,042
Ah, right.

311
00:17:44,418 --> 00:17:45,503
[♪ music fades]

312
00:17:48,130 --> 00:17:50,091
[footsteps approaching, heels clicking]

313
00:17:51,133 --> 00:17:55,513
Thank you all for joining us at
the Juyeon Arts High School Arts Festival.

314
00:17:55,596 --> 00:17:57,098
Juyeon Arts High School

315
00:17:57,181 --> 00:18:01,435
has grown into a prestigious school
known for producing exceptional dancers,

316
00:18:01,519 --> 00:18:04,605
and we owe much of that success
to one special person.

317
00:18:04,689 --> 00:18:08,192
I'd like to introduce you all
to Principal Jeong Joohee,

318
00:18:08,275 --> 00:18:10,945
who leads our school
with nothing but love for her students.

319
00:18:11,028 --> 00:18:12,405
[all applauding, cheering]

320
00:18:19,161 --> 00:18:20,246
Whoo!

321
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:28,295
[all applauding, cheering loudly]

322
00:18:31,257 --> 00:18:32,591
[applauding, cheering fades]

323
00:18:32,675 --> 00:18:36,721
I'd like to thank our distinguished guests
for taking the time to join us today.

324
00:18:37,638 --> 00:18:41,058
Recently, a tragic event
befell our school.

325
00:18:42,059 --> 00:18:46,564
Despite their grief, our students
worked hard to prepare this performance.

326
00:18:47,690 --> 00:18:49,316
I would be grateful

327
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:51,986
if you could give them
your warmest support.

328
00:18:53,028 --> 00:18:54,363
[all applauding]

329
00:18:58,451 --> 00:18:59,702
[applauding fades]

330
00:19:04,623 --> 00:19:06,250
WHEN A NAME BECOMES A GENRE OF ITS OWN

331
00:19:06,333 --> 00:19:08,043
[♪ upbeat, dramatic music playing]

332
00:19:11,839 --> 00:19:14,759
JEONG JOOHEE, THE DANCER
WHO HAS DEFINED AN ERA OF KOREAN DANCE

333
00:19:20,139 --> 00:19:21,348
HER NAME IS NOW A DIRECTION

334
00:19:23,976 --> 00:19:26,228
THE REASON KOREAN DANCE
KEPT MOVING FORWARD

335
00:19:27,855 --> 00:19:29,523
NOW SHE FOCUSES ON NURTURING TALENT

336
00:19:29,607 --> 00:19:30,983
[all applauding]

337
00:19:32,401 --> 00:19:34,069
AN EDUCATOR OF BOTH DANCE AND CHARACTER

338
00:19:34,153 --> 00:19:36,155
AN ICON SETTING THE STANDARD
FOR THE NEXT GENERATION

339
00:19:36,238 --> 00:19:40,367
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL
WILL CARRY ON HER LEGACY

340
00:19:40,910 --> 00:19:42,328
-[video, music stop abruptly]
-[projector clicks]

341
00:19:42,411 --> 00:19:43,788
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

342
00:19:43,871 --> 00:19:45,080
[utility knife clicking]

343
00:19:45,164 --> 00:19:46,916
-[slices]
-[all gasp]

344
00:19:48,375 --> 00:19:49,960
[all murmuring anxiously]

345
00:19:55,466 --> 00:19:56,675
[anxious murmuring intensifies]

346
00:20:00,304 --> 00:20:02,890
Mr. Park, what's going on?
Turn that off right now!

347
00:20:03,682 --> 00:20:04,892
-[radio clicks off]
-[audience exclaiming]

348
00:20:04,975 --> 00:20:06,435
It's okay.

349
00:20:09,355 --> 00:20:10,898
[audience gasping, exclaiming]

350
00:20:10,981 --> 00:20:12,274
[mic thuds, whines]

351
00:20:15,486 --> 00:20:16,695
[students scream]

352
00:20:17,446 --> 00:20:19,365
[panting] Girls.

353
00:20:19,448 --> 00:20:20,950
This isn't real.

354
00:20:21,033 --> 00:20:22,576
It's all fake.

355
00:20:32,378 --> 00:20:34,088
[audience murmuring anxiously]

356
00:20:37,633 --> 00:20:39,301
[panting frantically]

357
00:20:45,724 --> 00:20:47,142
[Juhee sighs, whimpers]

358
00:20:47,685 --> 00:20:49,603
[audience continues murmuring]

359
00:20:52,523 --> 00:20:53,858
[breath trembles] No.

360
00:20:53,941 --> 00:20:55,734
It's all a lie.

361
00:20:55,818 --> 00:20:57,111
You're a murderer.

362
00:20:57,194 --> 00:20:59,238
It's on video.
What do you mean it's a lie?

363
00:20:59,321 --> 00:21:01,490
[audience members jeering]

364
00:21:01,574 --> 00:21:03,868
[gasping sharply, yelling]
I said, it's not true!

365
00:21:04,493 --> 00:21:05,536
[♪ ominous music playing]

366
00:21:07,121 --> 00:21:08,205
[spectral exhale]

367
00:21:09,290 --> 00:21:10,416
[softly] Girls.

368
00:21:11,917 --> 00:21:13,627
[whimpering shakily]

369
00:21:13,711 --> 00:21:15,087
[gasping sharply]

370
00:21:15,170 --> 00:21:16,672
[whimpering shakily]

371
00:21:20,301 --> 00:21:21,844
[audience murmuring anxiously]

372
00:21:27,892 --> 00:21:29,476
[♪ music swells]

373
00:21:33,981 --> 00:21:35,316
[whimpering shakily, gasps]

374
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:37,693
[thuds]

375
00:21:37,776 --> 00:21:39,236
[audience exclaiming]

376
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:45,034
[spectator] Shouldn't we
call an ambulance?

377
00:21:45,117 --> 00:21:46,702
[all murmuring anxiously]

378
00:21:46,785 --> 00:21:48,662
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

379
00:21:53,959 --> 00:21:57,004
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

380
00:22:06,013 --> 00:22:07,306
Why did you kill her?

381
00:22:09,767 --> 00:22:10,935
Baek Yuna.

382
00:22:15,564 --> 00:22:17,232
She didn't know her place.

383
00:22:21,195 --> 00:22:22,279
[♪ music fades]

384
00:22:22,363 --> 00:22:23,489
[Yuna] <i>Ms. Jeong.</i>

385
00:22:23,572 --> 00:22:24,698
7 MONTHS AGO

386
00:22:24,782 --> 00:22:25,866
Am I not talented?

387
00:22:25,950 --> 00:22:26,951
[scoffs]

388
00:22:27,034 --> 00:22:28,327
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

389
00:22:28,410 --> 00:22:29,954
What are you talking about?

390
00:22:30,037 --> 00:22:32,498
You're exceptionally gifted.

391
00:22:32,581 --> 00:22:34,917
Then why did you take money from my mom?

392
00:22:36,502 --> 00:22:38,587
Did I get the lead because of the money?

393
00:22:39,380 --> 00:22:42,007
You even told her
you'd get me into college no matter what.

394
00:22:42,091 --> 00:22:44,259
That's not playing fair.

395
00:22:45,177 --> 00:22:46,178
[scoffs softly]

396
00:22:48,347 --> 00:22:49,515
Yuna.

397
00:22:51,976 --> 00:22:53,435
Having money

398
00:22:55,521 --> 00:22:56,981
is a talent.

399
00:22:58,148 --> 00:23:00,317
You're probably too young to understand.

400
00:23:00,401 --> 00:23:01,694
Playing fair?

401
00:23:02,861 --> 00:23:04,113
That's all an illusion.

402
00:23:04,905 --> 00:23:06,740
Nothing is fair in this world.

403
00:23:07,366 --> 00:23:09,201
Everything's decided
the moment you're born.

404
00:23:09,284 --> 00:23:10,577
Just like your genes.

405
00:23:11,370 --> 00:23:14,331
You can't last in this industry
without money anyway.

406
00:23:14,999 --> 00:23:17,501
So stop being so childish,

407
00:23:17,584 --> 00:23:20,379
and just enjoy the benefits
of having wealthy parents, huh?

408
00:23:22,715 --> 00:23:23,716
I don't want to.

409
00:23:25,884 --> 00:23:26,885
What?

410
00:23:28,220 --> 00:23:30,139
I want to be recognized for my own talent.

411
00:23:30,222 --> 00:23:31,265
[scoffs softly]

412
00:23:32,641 --> 00:23:34,309
What are you going to do about it?

413
00:23:34,935 --> 00:23:36,103
Turn yourself in.

414
00:23:37,021 --> 00:23:38,981
Otherwise, I'm going to report you myself.

415
00:23:44,737 --> 00:23:46,030
[♪ music swells]

416
00:23:47,114 --> 00:23:48,157
[door opens]

417
00:23:48,991 --> 00:23:50,034
[door closes]

418
00:23:51,368 --> 00:23:52,411
[♪ music fades]

419
00:23:54,955 --> 00:23:56,457
[cell phone vibrating]

420
00:23:59,043 --> 00:24:00,794
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

421
00:24:03,839 --> 00:24:05,257
Yes, Ms. Ryu.

422
00:24:05,340 --> 00:24:08,343
<i>Hello, Principal Jeong.</i>
<i>Have you been well?</i>

423
00:24:08,886 --> 00:24:09,970
Yes.

424
00:24:10,054 --> 00:24:13,932
<i>I have the bag you mentioned last time.</i>

425
00:24:14,016 --> 00:24:15,517
<i>I'll stop by to see you soon.</i>

426
00:24:16,143 --> 00:24:17,227
Ah.

427
00:24:17,811 --> 00:24:19,021
Yes, all right.

428
00:24:22,149 --> 00:24:23,192
[line disconnects]

429
00:24:23,275 --> 00:24:25,402
[♪ tense, foreboding music continues]

430
00:24:31,742 --> 00:24:34,161
You came to practice. [chuckles]

431
00:24:34,244 --> 00:24:35,579
You changed your mind, right?

432
00:24:36,747 --> 00:24:38,373
You made the right choice.

433
00:24:38,457 --> 00:24:41,085
Acting all righteous
won't do you any good.

434
00:24:53,597 --> 00:24:54,848
[♪ music fades]

435
00:24:54,932 --> 00:24:56,683
I came to practice one last time.

436
00:24:57,351 --> 00:24:58,352
One last time?

437
00:24:58,435 --> 00:25:00,354
Turn yourself in by tomorrow.

438
00:25:01,396 --> 00:25:02,898
I'm going to quit everything, too.

439
00:25:02,981 --> 00:25:04,900
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

440
00:25:35,472 --> 00:25:36,557
[seat belt unbuckles]

441
00:25:54,116 --> 00:25:55,242
[spectral exhale]

442
00:25:57,202 --> 00:25:59,079
[♪ ominous music playing]

443
00:26:04,835 --> 00:26:05,836
[clicking]

444
00:26:05,919 --> 00:26:07,379
[♪ ominous sting]

445
00:26:08,422 --> 00:26:09,965
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

446
00:26:22,227 --> 00:26:23,604
[spectral exhale]

447
00:26:23,687 --> 00:26:25,522
[♪ woman vocalizing gently]

448
00:26:34,656 --> 00:26:36,116
[♪ vocalizing, music fades]

449
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:38,035
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

450
00:26:45,542 --> 00:26:47,002
[sniffling, crying]

451
00:26:54,927 --> 00:26:56,553
[sniffles, breath trembles]

452
00:27:00,724 --> 00:27:02,142
Yuna.

453
00:27:03,894 --> 00:27:06,021
I know how you feel. [inhales shakily]

454
00:27:06,104 --> 00:27:07,856
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

455
00:27:10,359 --> 00:27:12,152
[exhales softly]
It's all been so hard on you.

456
00:27:12,986 --> 00:27:14,905
You haven't been able to sleep,

457
00:27:14,988 --> 00:27:17,824
and I heard
you're even taking antidepressants.

458
00:27:17,908 --> 00:27:19,409
[voice shaking] Ms. Jeong.

459
00:27:23,121 --> 00:27:25,332
You love dancing.

460
00:27:25,415 --> 00:27:28,251
How could you give it up, right?

461
00:27:38,095 --> 00:27:40,555
I'm taking antidepressants because of you.

462
00:27:41,264 --> 00:27:43,058
I've known for a while

463
00:27:43,892 --> 00:27:45,227
that my mom gave you money.

464
00:27:46,895 --> 00:27:49,106
I thought about looking the other way,

465
00:27:49,189 --> 00:27:52,359
because my mom and I would
also be blamed if this got out.

466
00:27:53,777 --> 00:27:55,862
[breathes shakily] Yuna.

467
00:27:57,739 --> 00:27:59,741
This won't be for long.

468
00:27:59,825 --> 00:28:01,410
If you just get through this,

469
00:28:02,619 --> 00:28:05,414
you'll become the best dancer there is.

470
00:28:05,497 --> 00:28:06,915
[♪ tense, melancholy music playing]

471
00:28:06,999 --> 00:28:08,417
[Juhee's breath trembling]

472
00:28:16,258 --> 00:28:18,301
I don't want to end up like you.

473
00:28:22,514 --> 00:28:23,515
What?

474
00:28:23,598 --> 00:28:24,933
Ms. Jeong.

475
00:28:25,726 --> 00:28:28,311
dance was the one thing I loved most,
and you corrupted it.

476
00:28:37,279 --> 00:28:38,530
Take back what you just said.

477
00:28:40,949 --> 00:28:42,576
If you say you're sorry,

478
00:28:44,578 --> 00:28:46,079
I'll forgive you just this once.

479
00:28:47,456 --> 00:28:48,498
I'm...

480
00:28:49,583 --> 00:28:50,959
giving you a chance.

481
00:28:51,668 --> 00:28:52,836
No.

482
00:28:52,919 --> 00:28:54,588
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

483
00:28:55,881 --> 00:28:57,049
Let go.

484
00:28:57,132 --> 00:28:58,508
[utility knife clicking]

485
00:28:59,092 --> 00:29:00,093
[Juhee grunts]

486
00:29:00,177 --> 00:29:02,179
[gasps incredulously, breathing heavily]

487
00:29:02,262 --> 00:29:03,346
[utility knife clatters]

488
00:29:03,972 --> 00:29:05,182
[breath trembling] Ms. Jeong.

489
00:29:05,766 --> 00:29:07,142
[Juhee] Don't resent me.

490
00:29:08,852 --> 00:29:11,021
You made me do this.

491
00:29:11,104 --> 00:29:12,397
[♪ music swells]

492
00:29:16,109 --> 00:29:17,444
[♪ music resumes tempo]

493
00:29:18,570 --> 00:29:20,655
[breathing raggedly]

494
00:29:37,672 --> 00:29:39,174
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

495
00:29:39,257 --> 00:29:40,592
[grunts, gasps]

496
00:29:41,009 --> 00:29:43,345
[continues breathing raggedly]

497
00:29:47,974 --> 00:29:49,726
[♪ music increases in tempo]

498
00:29:53,063 --> 00:29:54,147
[gasping sharply]

499
00:30:02,531 --> 00:30:03,740
[groans softly]

500
00:30:13,041 --> 00:30:14,084
[whimpers weakly]

501
00:30:14,167 --> 00:30:15,877
[♪ music swells]

502
00:30:25,220 --> 00:30:26,638
[♪ music resumes tempo]

503
00:30:30,183 --> 00:30:32,144
She's like this until the end.
[clicks tongue]

504
00:30:32,227 --> 00:30:34,396
JEONG JOOHEE

505
00:30:34,479 --> 00:30:35,939
[♪ music increases in tempo]

506
00:31:10,807 --> 00:31:15,854
I CURSE YOU

507
00:31:15,937 --> 00:31:19,149
-[♪ music resumes tempo]
-[Yuna] <i>Mom, I'm sorry.</i>

508
00:31:25,155 --> 00:31:26,281
[♪ music fades]

509
00:31:26,990 --> 00:31:28,033
[crying softly]

510
00:31:30,744 --> 00:31:32,329
It was killing me, too.

511
00:31:34,539 --> 00:31:37,709
Yuna haunted my dreams every night,
and I couldn't sleep.

512
00:31:39,169 --> 00:31:40,879
No medication would work,

513
00:31:43,006 --> 00:31:44,883
and I even turned to drugs because of her.

514
00:31:44,966 --> 00:31:46,760
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

515
00:31:47,719 --> 00:31:49,304
But then,

516
00:31:53,850 --> 00:31:56,436
there was another student
who didn't know her place.

517
00:32:06,363 --> 00:32:07,447
[glass clinks]

518
00:32:09,241 --> 00:32:10,325
[exhales sharply]

519
00:32:10,408 --> 00:32:11,576
[breathing deeply]

520
00:32:17,958 --> 00:32:20,001
-[knock at door]
-[gasps softly]

521
00:32:20,085 --> 00:32:21,253
[door opens]

522
00:32:22,420 --> 00:32:23,672
[♪ music fades]

523
00:32:24,339 --> 00:32:25,840
-Oh.
-[door closes]

524
00:32:26,466 --> 00:32:29,135
It's you, Seyeon. What can I do for you?

525
00:32:29,761 --> 00:32:32,931
I have something to tell you.

526
00:32:34,224 --> 00:32:36,685
I'm a bit busy right now.
Let's talk another time.

527
00:32:40,605 --> 00:32:42,315
This won't take long.

528
00:32:42,857 --> 00:32:45,360
What is it? Make it quick.

529
00:32:47,487 --> 00:32:50,365
I wish I could give you
a lot of money as well,

530
00:32:51,616 --> 00:32:53,618
but my family isn't well-off.

531
00:32:55,495 --> 00:32:57,622
I can't even afford private lessons.

532
00:33:00,667 --> 00:33:05,463
So I was secretly recording
your tutoring sessions with Yuna.

533
00:33:07,132 --> 00:33:08,633
[♪ ominous music playing]

534
00:33:31,406 --> 00:33:33,533
-[utility knife slices]
-[Yuna gasps incredulously]

535
00:33:34,743 --> 00:33:36,119
[utility knife clatters over recording]

536
00:33:36,494 --> 00:33:38,204
[Yuna, breath trembling]

537
00:33:38,288 --> 00:33:40,040
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

538
00:33:44,169 --> 00:33:45,879
[sighs softly] You know,

539
00:33:47,047 --> 00:33:49,382
I'd actually given up on everything.

540
00:33:51,092 --> 00:33:54,346
Only five students can go to
Hankuk University from our department.

541
00:33:54,429 --> 00:33:57,265
And they'll all be students
from rich, powerful families.

542
00:34:00,518 --> 00:34:02,354
Whereas I have nothing.

543
00:34:05,190 --> 00:34:07,442
But then this opportunity came along.

544
00:34:10,236 --> 00:34:11,571
[chuckles nervously]

545
00:34:13,406 --> 00:34:14,783
[stuttering] Seyeon.

546
00:34:16,785 --> 00:34:18,912
Does anyone else know about this?

547
00:34:19,913 --> 00:34:22,999
[chuckles] Of course not.
No one else can know.

548
00:34:23,083 --> 00:34:25,085
I can't have you getting arrested.

549
00:34:25,168 --> 00:34:26,419
Seyeon,

550
00:34:27,462 --> 00:34:29,422
you can't do this. Delete that right now.

551
00:34:29,506 --> 00:34:31,424
Can a teacher kill her student?

552
00:34:33,843 --> 00:34:37,389
All you have to do
is favor me from now on.

553
00:34:41,142 --> 00:34:43,353
Start by making me
the lead dancer in the festival.

554
00:34:46,398 --> 00:34:49,025
Don't even think about trying anything.

555
00:34:50,860 --> 00:34:53,988
I'm not like Yuna.
I won't be easy to deal with.

556
00:34:58,159 --> 00:34:59,411
[♪ music increases in tempo]

557
00:35:00,245 --> 00:35:01,329
[scoffs]

558
00:35:02,372 --> 00:35:04,749
I'll keep this nice and safe
so no one finds out.

559
00:35:04,833 --> 00:35:05,959
Don't worry about that.

560
00:35:07,335 --> 00:35:09,796
I'll delete it
once I get into Hankuk University.

561
00:35:11,339 --> 00:35:12,674
[♪ music swells]

562
00:35:15,260 --> 00:35:18,054
[door opens, closes]

563
00:35:18,805 --> 00:35:19,848
[♪ music fades]

564
00:35:19,931 --> 00:35:22,684
So I did exactly as Seyeon asked,

565
00:35:25,437 --> 00:35:29,441
but the parents of the student originally
chosen for the lead kept calling me.

566
00:35:30,692 --> 00:35:34,571
They kept hounding me
about how much Seyeon had paid me.

567
00:35:36,322 --> 00:35:38,616
You even killed someone
after taking a bribe,

568
00:35:39,743 --> 00:35:41,119
yet you accepted money again?

569
00:35:42,287 --> 00:35:44,122
You think I asked for it?

570
00:35:44,205 --> 00:35:46,124
They come to me on their own.

571
00:35:46,833 --> 00:35:50,420
They come with designer bags and cash,
asking me to look after their kid.

572
00:35:50,503 --> 00:35:52,964
Is that why you decided
to kill Seyeon as well?

573
00:35:53,047 --> 00:35:54,924
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

574
00:35:55,759 --> 00:35:56,760
[inhales sharply]

575
00:35:58,762 --> 00:36:02,098
That wasn't my intention from the start.

576
00:36:02,849 --> 00:36:03,933
I was...

577
00:36:05,435 --> 00:36:07,228
just wondering what I should do,

578
00:36:08,021 --> 00:36:09,105
then...

579
00:36:10,607 --> 00:36:12,901
I went online to get some drugs.

580
00:36:12,984 --> 00:36:14,903
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

581
00:36:15,445 --> 00:36:16,529
[exhales softly]

582
00:36:22,035 --> 00:36:25,038
GOT SOMETHING NEW, WANNA TRY?

583
00:36:25,121 --> 00:36:27,290
WHAT IS IT?

584
00:36:27,373 --> 00:36:29,167
SOMETHING THAT FEELS GOOD
JUST BY TOUCHING IT

585
00:36:29,250 --> 00:36:30,627
BUT BAD FOR HEART CONDITION OR ASTHMA

586
00:36:31,211 --> 00:36:33,421
[keyboard clacking]

587
00:36:33,505 --> 00:36:36,841
WHY? WHAT HAPPENS?

588
00:36:37,509 --> 00:36:40,261
WORST CASE, YOU DIE

589
00:36:40,345 --> 00:36:43,056
[♪ ominous sting]

590
00:36:44,557 --> 00:36:45,892
[♪ music resumes tempo]

591
00:36:47,769 --> 00:36:48,853
[door opens]

592
00:36:51,272 --> 00:36:53,316
-[student 1] Hello.
-[student 2] Hello.

593
00:36:53,399 --> 00:36:54,484
Warm up.

594
00:36:58,530 --> 00:36:59,572
[sighs softly]

595
00:37:01,032 --> 00:37:02,325
[♪ music turns ominous]

596
00:37:12,252 --> 00:37:14,671
-[switch clicks]
-Warm up and start rehearsing.

597
00:37:14,754 --> 00:37:15,880
-Yes, ma'am.
-[students] Yes, ma'am.

598
00:37:17,882 --> 00:37:19,008
MOON SEYEON

599
00:37:25,223 --> 00:37:26,850
[♪ music increases in tempo]

600
00:37:35,525 --> 00:37:37,360
[♪ ominous, ticking music playing]

601
00:37:46,160 --> 00:37:47,579
[♪ music swells]

602
00:37:53,543 --> 00:37:54,878
[♪ music resumes tempo]

603
00:37:54,961 --> 00:37:56,713
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

604
00:38:08,057 --> 00:38:09,309
[spectral whoosh]

605
00:38:09,934 --> 00:38:11,227
[spectral exhale]

606
00:38:12,687 --> 00:38:14,480
[♪ percussive folk music playing]

607
00:38:15,315 --> 00:38:16,482
[blade swooshing]

608
00:38:19,110 --> 00:38:20,653
-[♪ music stops]
-[panting]

609
00:38:22,238 --> 00:38:23,489
[♪ music turns ominous]

610
00:38:29,245 --> 00:38:30,288
[Yuna] Seyeon.

611
00:38:30,371 --> 00:38:32,582
Please... help me.

612
00:38:32,665 --> 00:38:34,167
-[spectral exhale]
-[sword clatters]

613
00:38:35,710 --> 00:38:37,545
Don't come any closer.

614
00:38:37,629 --> 00:38:38,713
Stay away from me!

615
00:38:38,796 --> 00:38:41,799
Seyeon, please help me.

616
00:38:41,883 --> 00:38:43,217
[screaming]

617
00:38:43,301 --> 00:38:44,594
[blunt thudding]

618
00:38:44,677 --> 00:38:46,387
[continues screaming]

619
00:38:50,475 --> 00:38:51,893
[gasping frantically, grunting]

620
00:38:53,353 --> 00:38:55,438
[♪ music swells, fades]

621
00:38:55,521 --> 00:38:57,357
-[wheezing heavily]
-[sword clatters]

622
00:38:58,024 --> 00:38:59,859
[♪ soft, somber music playing]

623
00:38:59,943 --> 00:39:01,194
[wheezing, choking]

624
00:39:07,992 --> 00:39:10,328
[Isoo] You're the one who slipped
Gaeun the drugs as well, right?

625
00:39:12,038 --> 00:39:14,999
To make it look like
an incident between the students.

626
00:39:15,083 --> 00:39:17,085
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

627
00:39:18,962 --> 00:39:19,963
SONG GAEUN

628
00:39:26,177 --> 00:39:27,220
[scoffs]

629
00:39:27,804 --> 00:39:28,888
[♪ music fades]

630
00:39:28,972 --> 00:39:30,598
You really are something else.

631
00:39:32,266 --> 00:39:34,602
As a teacher,
you killed two of your students.

632
00:39:35,979 --> 00:39:37,897
How can you live with that?

633
00:39:37,981 --> 00:39:41,567
[inhales sharply] What else could I
have done? There was no other way.

634
00:39:41,651 --> 00:39:42,777
[breath trembles]

635
00:39:43,903 --> 00:39:46,406
They blackmailed me first,

636
00:39:46,489 --> 00:39:47,949
so this was self-defense.

637
00:39:48,032 --> 00:39:50,952
If you had just admitted your crime,
no one would have died.

638
00:39:51,035 --> 00:39:52,078
[scoffs]

639
00:39:52,161 --> 00:39:53,371
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

640
00:39:53,454 --> 00:39:55,623
Who in the world would do that?

641
00:39:55,707 --> 00:39:57,917
[yelling] I have a name
and a reputation to uphold!

642
00:39:58,001 --> 00:40:00,336
You're the one
who tarnished that reputation.

643
00:40:00,420 --> 00:40:02,046
Now, people will remember you

644
00:40:03,131 --> 00:40:05,675
not as the legend of Korean dance,

645
00:40:07,093 --> 00:40:08,845
but as a murderer.

646
00:40:16,060 --> 00:40:17,228
[sobbing softly]

647
00:40:22,608 --> 00:40:24,569
MOON SEYEON, MAY YOU REST IN PEACE

648
00:40:26,446 --> 00:40:28,114
[♪ somber, melancholy music playing]

649
00:40:28,197 --> 00:40:29,657
WE WILL MISS YOU, SEYEON

650
00:40:34,620 --> 00:40:35,913
[sniffling, sobbing]

651
00:40:39,834 --> 00:40:40,835
[sniffles]

652
00:40:46,507 --> 00:40:48,718
My poor child. [sobbing bitterly]

653
00:40:55,224 --> 00:40:57,268
My poor child.

654
00:40:59,103 --> 00:41:00,646
[♪ music increases in tempo]

655
00:41:05,693 --> 00:41:06,944
PRINCIPAL JEONG JOOHEE

656
00:41:15,703 --> 00:41:16,788
[shattering]

657
00:41:24,337 --> 00:41:25,338
[♪ music fades]

658
00:41:28,382 --> 00:41:29,884
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

659
00:41:47,777 --> 00:41:48,820
[♪ music fades]

660
00:41:48,903 --> 00:41:49,904
CURSE CHARM

661
00:41:49,987 --> 00:41:51,614
JUNYOUNG, KYUNGJIN
I CURSE YOU, BREAK UP

662
00:41:55,451 --> 00:41:56,452
Where's everyone?

663
00:41:56,536 --> 00:41:58,287
Off to meet their girlfriends. [sighs]

664
00:41:58,371 --> 00:42:00,665
Such romantics, aren't they?

665
00:42:00,748 --> 00:42:01,791
[chuckles softly]

666
00:42:02,625 --> 00:42:04,877
Why don't us single folks
go get something to eat?

667
00:42:04,961 --> 00:42:07,380
Shall we go somewhere I know?
It's Michelin-starred.

668
00:42:07,463 --> 00:42:09,048
-Let's just go local. I'm hungry.
-[mouse clicking]

669
00:42:09,132 --> 00:42:11,634
You must have
a bottomless pit for a stomach.

670
00:42:11,717 --> 00:42:13,136
Wrap it up quickly.

671
00:42:14,137 --> 00:42:15,138
Oh, I'm starving.

672
00:42:16,722 --> 00:42:18,057
I just need to finish this.

673
00:42:22,478 --> 00:42:23,980
[crunching]

674
00:42:29,735 --> 00:42:31,571
Mmm! It's delicious.

675
00:42:31,654 --> 00:42:33,114
-It's good, right?
-Yeah.

676
00:42:33,197 --> 00:42:34,907
This is the best place around here.

677
00:42:34,991 --> 00:42:37,910
Why go to a Michelin restaurant
when we have a place like this?

678
00:42:37,994 --> 00:42:40,329
Hey, Michelin is Michelin, so...

679
00:42:41,080 --> 00:42:44,083
[sighs in exasperation] Forget it.
Want a draft beer?

680
00:42:44,167 --> 00:42:45,459
Yeah, sounds good.

681
00:42:45,543 --> 00:42:48,421
Can we have two...
No, one glass of draft beer, please.

682
00:42:48,504 --> 00:42:49,505
[server] Sure.

683
00:42:52,717 --> 00:42:53,843
Mmm!

684
00:42:53,926 --> 00:42:54,927
That's good.

685
00:42:55,636 --> 00:42:59,015
By the way, that reed you gave me.

686
00:42:59,932 --> 00:43:01,058
Yeah?

687
00:43:01,142 --> 00:43:04,020
Apparently, they can't determine
the exact location with that,

688
00:43:04,103 --> 00:43:06,063
because it's native to the west coast.

689
00:43:06,147 --> 00:43:07,732
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

690
00:43:08,566 --> 00:43:10,359
What are you going to do about Seongwon?

691
00:43:11,027 --> 00:43:12,403
I have someone watching him.

692
00:43:13,070 --> 00:43:14,989
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

693
00:43:23,372 --> 00:43:24,832
[Mr. Hwang] Welcome home, Young Master.

694
00:43:43,601 --> 00:43:44,602
[door closes]

695
00:43:46,771 --> 00:43:47,939
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

696
00:43:48,022 --> 00:43:49,148
[keyboard clacking]

697
00:43:57,865 --> 00:43:58,908
Thank you.

698
00:43:59,784 --> 00:44:00,868
[cell phone vibrating]

699
00:44:00,952 --> 00:44:02,912
PI JEONG MINJAE

700
00:44:03,621 --> 00:44:04,622
Hello?

701
00:44:04,705 --> 00:44:06,582
Yu Seongwon brought a woman to his studio.

702
00:44:06,666 --> 00:44:07,667
I'll head there first.

703
00:44:07,750 --> 00:44:09,585
Okay, we're on our way.

704
00:44:09,669 --> 00:44:11,379
-[line disconnects]
-What's wrong?

705
00:44:11,462 --> 00:44:13,965
Yu Seongwon brought a woman to his studio.

706
00:44:14,048 --> 00:44:15,174
[♪ music swells]

707
00:44:17,218 --> 00:44:18,219
[♪ music fades]

708
00:44:22,848 --> 00:44:25,309
[Areum] Your studio is really nice.

709
00:44:26,811 --> 00:44:29,689
[sighs] I wish I could work
in a studio like this.

710
00:44:32,024 --> 00:44:34,360
You can work here anytime you want.

711
00:44:35,152 --> 00:44:37,238
-Really?
-Of course.

712
00:44:38,656 --> 00:44:39,991
[giggles excitedly]

713
00:44:43,411 --> 00:44:45,288
If you can make it here.

714
00:44:45,371 --> 00:44:47,039
[♪ ominous music playing]

715
00:44:56,215 --> 00:44:58,217
-[camera shutter clicking]
-Why do you take photographs?

716
00:44:58,301 --> 00:45:00,928
To feel you while I work.

717
00:45:01,846 --> 00:45:03,806
Can I get a copy if they come out well?

718
00:45:05,057 --> 00:45:06,309
[chuckles softly]

719
00:45:06,392 --> 00:45:07,393
No.

720
00:45:10,438 --> 00:45:12,732
What kind of artwork
are you going to make me into?

721
00:45:12,815 --> 00:45:14,775
I'm not sure. [sighs softly]

722
00:45:14,859 --> 00:45:16,569
I can't say I know you yet.

723
00:45:17,403 --> 00:45:18,988
What do you like most?

724
00:45:19,071 --> 00:45:21,365
I like painting the most.

725
00:45:21,449 --> 00:45:22,950
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

726
00:45:23,034 --> 00:45:24,452
I wish I could

727
00:45:25,286 --> 00:45:28,414
spend just one month painting,
without worrying about money.

728
00:45:29,040 --> 00:45:30,041
[scoffs]

729
00:45:31,042 --> 00:45:32,335
That's no fun.

730
00:45:33,127 --> 00:45:34,670
What's no fun?

731
00:45:36,464 --> 00:45:38,215
[♪ music increases in tempo]

732
00:45:54,357 --> 00:45:55,524
[liquid squirting]

733
00:46:01,405 --> 00:46:03,115
-[camera shutter clicks]
-Talk about something else.

734
00:46:03,866 --> 00:46:06,243
What was the worst thing you've ever done?

735
00:46:06,827 --> 00:46:08,913
[chuckles softly] The worst thing?

736
00:46:08,996 --> 00:46:09,997
[♪ music fades]

737
00:46:11,540 --> 00:46:12,750
What about you?

738
00:46:12,833 --> 00:46:15,711
The worst thing I've done?

739
00:46:15,795 --> 00:46:17,630
[♪ ominous music playing]

740
00:46:20,591 --> 00:46:21,967
You'd be shocked if you knew.

741
00:46:23,386 --> 00:46:24,595
What was it?

742
00:46:29,433 --> 00:46:30,935
I gave my father

743
00:46:31,769 --> 00:46:33,229
a makeover.

744
00:46:37,817 --> 00:46:38,984
Your father?

745
00:46:39,068 --> 00:46:42,571
I put really heavy makeup on him.

746
00:46:45,783 --> 00:46:47,159
[♪ music swells]

747
00:46:49,495 --> 00:46:50,788
-[♪ music resumes tempo]
-Why?

748
00:46:52,790 --> 00:46:54,583
Because I didn't like his expression.

749
00:46:54,667 --> 00:46:55,835
[chuckles softly]

750
00:46:56,502 --> 00:46:58,254
Didn't he tell you off?

751
00:46:59,547 --> 00:47:00,923
He didn't say anything.

752
00:47:06,095 --> 00:47:07,221
[exhales softly]

753
00:47:08,639 --> 00:47:10,057
Want a glass of champagne?

754
00:47:10,683 --> 00:47:12,059
[♪ ominous music continues]

755
00:47:12,143 --> 00:47:13,602
[footsteps approaching]

756
00:47:14,145 --> 00:47:15,396
Any movements?

757
00:47:16,313 --> 00:47:17,356
Not yet.

758
00:47:22,445 --> 00:47:23,654
Should we go in now?

759
00:47:23,737 --> 00:47:25,531
No, let's just wait.

760
00:47:26,157 --> 00:47:27,908
[♪ music increases in tempo]

761
00:47:40,754 --> 00:47:42,882
[♪ ominous sting]

762
00:47:42,965 --> 00:47:44,383
How do you want to die?

763
00:47:45,259 --> 00:47:46,260
What?

764
00:47:46,343 --> 00:47:48,596
How do you want to die?

765
00:47:48,679 --> 00:47:50,222
Have you never thought about that?

766
00:47:51,015 --> 00:47:52,099
[chuckles softly]

767
00:47:52,183 --> 00:47:53,517
[♪ ominous sting]

768
00:47:53,601 --> 00:47:54,894
Well,

769
00:47:56,437 --> 00:47:59,356
I'd want to die painlessly and peacefully.

770
00:47:59,940 --> 00:48:00,941
Peacefully?

771
00:48:01,525 --> 00:48:03,444
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

772
00:48:07,490 --> 00:48:08,782
That's nice, too.

773
00:48:14,872 --> 00:48:16,040
Drink up.

774
00:48:20,461 --> 00:48:22,463
[♪ ominous, ticking music playing]

775
00:48:27,051 --> 00:48:28,260
[♪ music swells]

776
00:48:31,430 --> 00:48:32,598
[car horn blaring]

777
00:48:32,681 --> 00:48:34,391
-[♪ music fades]
-[car horn honking]

778
00:48:34,475 --> 00:48:36,519
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

779
00:48:36,602 --> 00:48:37,978
[car horn honking]

780
00:48:39,647 --> 00:48:41,857
[car horn honking, blaring]

781
00:48:49,281 --> 00:48:51,367
Young Master Isoo is here.

782
00:48:55,162 --> 00:48:56,330
[sighs deeply]

783
00:48:56,997 --> 00:48:58,165
[chuckles]

784
00:48:59,667 --> 00:49:01,168
We have an unwanted guest.

785
00:49:07,758 --> 00:49:09,969
Sorry to drop in so late. Can I come in?

786
00:49:10,052 --> 00:49:12,555
-Oh. Yes, of course.
-Thanks.

787
00:49:20,396 --> 00:49:22,731
[♪ music swells, fades]

788
00:49:27,152 --> 00:49:28,153
Isoo!

789
00:49:28,237 --> 00:49:30,155
What brings you here out of the blue?

790
00:49:30,239 --> 00:49:32,324
I just remembered you said you liked this.

791
00:49:33,033 --> 00:49:35,452
Here. We'll drink one bottle now.

792
00:49:35,536 --> 00:49:36,745
Thank you.

793
00:49:38,872 --> 00:49:40,124
You have a guest.

794
00:49:41,000 --> 00:49:43,002
Ah, you must be his model.

795
00:49:43,085 --> 00:49:46,547
[chuckles softly]
Yes. Aren't you Jin Isoo?

796
00:49:47,298 --> 00:49:49,633
She knows me. She must be a fan.

797
00:49:49,717 --> 00:49:51,176
Would you like a photo?

798
00:49:51,260 --> 00:49:52,553
-Really?
-Yes.

799
00:49:54,555 --> 00:49:55,639
All right.

800
00:49:56,390 --> 00:49:58,100
-One, two, three.
-[camera shutter clicks]

801
00:49:58,767 --> 00:50:00,936
Nice to meet you. What's your name?

802
00:50:01,020 --> 00:50:02,229
Song Areum.

803
00:50:02,313 --> 00:50:03,814
Areum.

804
00:50:03,897 --> 00:50:06,191
Would you like to join us for a drink?
I made this.

805
00:50:06,275 --> 00:50:07,276
No.

806
00:50:07,776 --> 00:50:08,819
Uh...

807
00:50:09,320 --> 00:50:11,447
Areum should probably get going.

808
00:50:12,323 --> 00:50:13,616
Let's do this another time.

809
00:50:13,699 --> 00:50:14,700
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

810
00:50:14,783 --> 00:50:15,868
[Areum] Ah.

811
00:50:16,243 --> 00:50:17,369
[chuckles softly]

812
00:50:17,453 --> 00:50:18,454
Okay, sure.

813
00:50:19,038 --> 00:50:21,457
Mmm, then I'll have to call you a cab.

814
00:50:21,540 --> 00:50:24,960
The premium kind. One second. Ah...

815
00:50:26,920 --> 00:50:28,255
Your cab's here.

816
00:50:28,339 --> 00:50:29,423
Wear your seatbelt.

817
00:50:29,506 --> 00:50:30,591
-Okay.
-Right.

818
00:50:30,674 --> 00:50:31,967
[exhales contentedly]

819
00:50:34,011 --> 00:50:35,638
You look like a skilled driver.

820
00:50:36,347 --> 00:50:38,641
Please take her home safely. Bye.

821
00:50:48,233 --> 00:50:50,194
Seriously, what the heck?

822
00:50:51,278 --> 00:50:53,822
What do you mean?
Come on, let's go have a drink.

823
00:50:53,906 --> 00:50:54,948
Let's go.

824
00:50:55,032 --> 00:50:56,325
[♪ music increases in tempo]

825
00:50:56,408 --> 00:50:57,534
Let's go!

826
00:51:07,711 --> 00:51:09,338
-[♪ music resumes tempo]
-[Hyera panting] Wait.

827
00:51:11,465 --> 00:51:12,591
I'm a detective.

828
00:51:12,675 --> 00:51:13,759
[♪ music fades]

829
00:51:15,177 --> 00:51:16,845
You were with Yu Seongwon, weren't you?

830
00:51:19,723 --> 00:51:20,724
Yes.

831
00:51:21,266 --> 00:51:22,476
What's going on?

832
00:51:23,018 --> 00:51:25,020
Could I talk to you for a second?

833
00:51:25,104 --> 00:51:27,356
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

834
00:51:27,439 --> 00:51:31,151
I work part-time as a bartender.
I met him at the bar.

835
00:51:31,235 --> 00:51:32,986
Did he ask you to be his model?

836
00:51:33,070 --> 00:51:34,196
Yes.

837
00:51:35,406 --> 00:51:37,491
But what's this all about?

838
00:51:38,075 --> 00:51:41,745
Two of Yu Seongwon's models are missing.

839
00:51:42,413 --> 00:51:44,206
What do you mean?

840
00:51:45,165 --> 00:51:46,709
We're investigating those cases.

841
00:51:46,792 --> 00:51:49,086
[♪ pulsating, suspenseful music playing]

842
00:51:49,169 --> 00:51:50,421
No wonder.

843
00:51:50,504 --> 00:51:53,966
He said something
that was kind of disturbing.

844
00:51:54,049 --> 00:51:55,300
Like what?

845
00:51:56,844 --> 00:51:58,637
How do you want to die?

846
00:51:58,721 --> 00:51:59,847
[Hyera exhales softly]

847
00:52:03,350 --> 00:52:05,978
You shouldn't meet him
even if he calls you again.

848
00:52:06,478 --> 00:52:07,479
Okay.

849
00:52:07,563 --> 00:52:08,897
If he contacts you,

850
00:52:08,981 --> 00:52:11,024
please let me know.

851
00:52:14,236 --> 00:52:15,362
[♪ music fades]

852
00:52:15,946 --> 00:52:17,114
[Isoo] Hey, are you mad at me?

853
00:52:17,781 --> 00:52:19,658
Who's more important to you,
me or the model?

854
00:52:19,742 --> 00:52:23,287
It's been a while
since I found a model I liked, Isoo.

855
00:52:23,370 --> 00:52:25,205
[sighs] Drink up.

856
00:52:25,289 --> 00:52:26,707
Get inspiration from me today.

857
00:52:28,208 --> 00:52:29,209
[clink]

858
00:52:32,588 --> 00:52:34,673
-Hey, Seongwon.
-Yeah?

859
00:52:34,757 --> 00:52:38,093
You said you met me when you were little.

860
00:52:38,177 --> 00:52:40,012
-Yeah.
-When was that?

861
00:52:40,971 --> 00:52:42,765
[sighs deeply] Seriously.

862
00:52:43,766 --> 00:52:46,351
It annoys me that you don't remember,
so I'm not telling you.

863
00:52:46,435 --> 00:52:48,854
At least give me a hint.

864
00:52:53,275 --> 00:52:54,818
Back then,

865
00:52:55,527 --> 00:52:57,404
you were a lot quieter than you are now.

866
00:52:59,490 --> 00:53:02,409
You were shorter and thinner.

867
00:53:02,493 --> 00:53:03,744
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

868
00:53:04,411 --> 00:53:06,079
The hallway was bright,

869
00:53:07,790 --> 00:53:10,375
and a breeze was coming in
through the window.

870
00:53:13,045 --> 00:53:14,171
SEO YUKYUNG PSYCHIATRIC CLINIC

871
00:53:14,254 --> 00:53:15,756
<i>It was quiet</i>

872
00:53:16,548 --> 00:53:17,966
<i>and dull.</i>

873
00:53:20,135 --> 00:53:24,473
<i>Surrounded by white walls,</i>
<i>it was the same thing day after day,</i>

874
00:53:29,144 --> 00:53:32,564
<i>but then, you suddenly sat next to me.</i>

875
00:53:32,648 --> 00:53:35,359
Hey, what's your name?

876
00:53:38,821 --> 00:53:40,072
What are you sick with?

877
00:53:45,410 --> 00:53:46,495
How's my drawing?

878
00:53:50,040 --> 00:53:51,291
It's really good.

879
00:53:51,375 --> 00:53:53,168
Do you know what this is?

880
00:53:53,877 --> 00:53:54,920
It's a puppy.

881
00:54:03,887 --> 00:54:05,722
[door opens]

882
00:54:05,806 --> 00:54:07,224
[Dr. Seo] Jin Isoo.

883
00:54:07,307 --> 00:54:08,600
Come inside.

884
00:54:19,820 --> 00:54:20,946
Jin Isoo.

885
00:54:25,868 --> 00:54:26,869
[chuckles softly]

886
00:54:28,662 --> 00:54:29,663
My picture.

887
00:54:30,497 --> 00:54:32,916
Everyone said it was weird.

888
00:54:33,000 --> 00:54:35,294
You were the only person
who complimented me.

889
00:54:42,384 --> 00:54:43,510
Do you know why?

890
00:54:44,761 --> 00:54:47,556
You recognized it
because you and I are alike.

891
00:54:49,391 --> 00:54:52,144
In what way are we alike?

892
00:54:52,227 --> 00:54:53,312
[exhales softly]

893
00:54:54,980 --> 00:54:56,148
Your mom.

894
00:54:58,650 --> 00:55:01,695
You said you were with her when she died.

895
00:55:02,279 --> 00:55:03,280
[Seongwon] Huh?

896
00:55:05,282 --> 00:55:06,575
How did it feel?

897
00:55:09,411 --> 00:55:11,747
Did you witness the moment she died?

898
00:55:12,539 --> 00:55:14,541
When her soul left her eyes?

899
00:55:15,417 --> 00:55:16,710
That very moment?

900
00:55:16,793 --> 00:55:18,003
[♪ music swells]

901
00:55:20,756 --> 00:55:22,007
[♪ music fades]

902
00:55:24,384 --> 00:55:25,427
[door opens]

903
00:55:26,428 --> 00:55:27,429
[door closes]

904
00:55:30,766 --> 00:55:32,267
This is Detective Jin Isoo.

905
00:55:32,351 --> 00:55:33,935
This is private investigator Jeong Minjae.

906
00:55:34,019 --> 00:55:35,979
He used to work at Violent Crime with me.

907
00:55:36,605 --> 00:55:37,939
Oh, it's nice to meet you.

908
00:55:38,565 --> 00:55:40,150
You really helped us out today.

909
00:55:40,233 --> 00:55:41,485
Not at all.

910
00:55:42,361 --> 00:55:43,862
So, what did Areum say?

911
00:55:44,446 --> 00:55:46,782
They met by chance,
and he asked her to be his model.

912
00:55:46,865 --> 00:55:47,866
[Isoo] Hmm.

913
00:55:48,617 --> 00:55:50,327
Did you talk to him?

914
00:55:50,410 --> 00:55:53,288
He said I met him when I was young,

915
00:55:53,372 --> 00:55:56,249
but I honestly don't remember.

916
00:55:59,961 --> 00:56:01,213
What are you going to do now?

917
00:56:01,922 --> 00:56:03,382
We'll have to keep watching.

918
00:56:04,132 --> 00:56:06,426
He might go on a rampage
now that we've stopped him.

919
00:56:07,010 --> 00:56:08,011
[Isoo sighs softly]

920
00:56:17,020 --> 00:56:18,146
[sighs softly]

921
00:56:18,230 --> 00:56:19,690
[footsteps approaching]

922
00:56:28,240 --> 00:56:30,158
[crockery clinking]

923
00:56:31,576 --> 00:56:32,744
[sighs wearily]

924
00:56:36,206 --> 00:56:38,125
I bring Areum home...

925
00:56:38,208 --> 00:56:39,960
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

926
00:56:43,630 --> 00:56:47,217
<i>-...and he barges in an hour later?</i>
<i>-</i>[car horn honking, blaring]

927
00:56:48,093 --> 00:56:49,094
[scoffs softly]

928
00:56:50,721 --> 00:56:51,847
That's strange.

929
00:56:52,723 --> 00:56:53,724
Right?

930
00:56:57,978 --> 00:56:59,479
[sighs deeply]

931
00:57:00,772 --> 00:57:02,065
[♪ music fades]

932
00:57:04,067 --> 00:57:05,068
[slurps]

933
00:57:05,902 --> 00:57:07,028
[exhales deeply]

934
00:57:08,739 --> 00:57:10,657
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

935
00:57:13,285 --> 00:57:14,286
What the heck?

936
00:57:23,920 --> 00:57:24,963
[sighs wearily]

937
00:57:25,046 --> 00:57:26,339
[♪ music swells]

938
00:57:30,635 --> 00:57:31,762
[sighs softly]

939
00:57:35,056 --> 00:57:36,057
[♪ music fades]

940
00:57:36,141 --> 00:57:37,184
Did Isoo...

941
00:57:39,019 --> 00:57:41,146
side with Joo Hyera?

942
00:57:41,229 --> 00:57:42,355
[♪ suspenseful sting]

943
00:57:46,485 --> 00:57:47,819
[cell phone ringing over car audio]

944
00:57:47,903 --> 00:57:49,488
DETECTIVE JOO HYERA
INCOMING CALL

945
00:57:50,989 --> 00:57:53,116
[Hyera] <i>Yu Seongwon found our cameras.</i>

946
00:57:53,200 --> 00:57:54,910
<i>He destroyed them all.</i>

947
00:57:54,993 --> 00:57:56,369
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

948
00:57:56,453 --> 00:57:57,871
We have no way of watching him.

949
00:58:00,582 --> 00:58:01,792
I'll look into it.

950
00:58:07,130 --> 00:58:08,173
MR. CHOI

951
00:58:08,256 --> 00:58:09,883
[line connects, ringing]

952
00:58:11,384 --> 00:58:13,595
[Isoo] Mr. Choi, I have a favor to ask.

953
00:58:13,678 --> 00:58:14,971
[engine revving]

954
00:58:19,226 --> 00:58:20,227
HANSU AIR SPACE

955
00:58:20,310 --> 00:58:21,561
[tires screeching]

956
00:58:24,022 --> 00:58:25,106
[♪ music fades]

957
00:58:25,190 --> 00:58:27,901
Ah, why did you come? I can go by myself.

958
00:58:27,984 --> 00:58:30,070
I thought I might as well come see you.

959
00:58:30,153 --> 00:58:31,530
How are you feeling?

960
00:58:31,613 --> 00:58:33,114
-[inhales sharply]
-[exhales sharply]

961
00:58:33,198 --> 00:58:34,491
It's a secret.

962
00:58:34,574 --> 00:58:35,575
[whispering] How are you?

963
00:58:35,659 --> 00:58:38,453
I'm fine. Don't worry about me.

964
00:58:38,537 --> 00:58:39,955
What did the hospital say?

965
00:58:40,038 --> 00:58:42,332
They're going to monitor me for a while,

966
00:58:42,415 --> 00:58:44,501
but I'm doing well so far.

967
00:58:44,584 --> 00:58:46,086
[sighs in relief] That's such a relief.

968
00:58:47,212 --> 00:58:48,880
What about you?

969
00:58:48,964 --> 00:58:51,716
I'm taking medication and doing okay.

970
00:58:51,800 --> 00:58:52,801
Really?

971
00:58:52,884 --> 00:58:55,762
Really. You should
worry about yourself first.

972
00:58:55,846 --> 00:58:57,097
[clicks tongue] Don't get sick.

973
00:58:58,348 --> 00:58:59,808
-Right.
-Let's go.

974
00:59:01,059 --> 00:59:02,686
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

975
00:59:10,026 --> 00:59:11,528
Thank you all for your hard work.

976
00:59:12,320 --> 00:59:14,239
Don't mind us. Please carry on.

977
00:59:16,783 --> 00:59:18,577
It's been a while, Chief.

978
00:59:20,328 --> 00:59:21,413
[♪ music fades]

979
00:59:24,082 --> 00:59:25,876
Yes, please move it

980
00:59:25,959 --> 00:59:27,627
right here.

981
00:59:27,711 --> 00:59:29,588
[♪ quirky music playing]

982
00:59:29,671 --> 00:59:31,756
What is it for?

983
00:59:31,840 --> 00:59:35,051
Uh, you'll be in danger if you know.

984
00:59:35,135 --> 00:59:37,137
Please set it up
so I can watch the live feed.

985
00:59:39,097 --> 00:59:40,515
Please do as he says.

986
00:59:42,934 --> 00:59:44,644
-[♪ music fades]
-So what exactly is this again?

987
00:59:44,728 --> 00:59:47,480
-Mmm, a high-altitude UAV.
-[keyboard clacking]

988
00:59:47,564 --> 00:59:49,608
A drone that can fly for a long time.

989
00:59:51,568 --> 00:59:53,194
And it belongs to Hansu Group?

990
00:59:54,112 --> 00:59:56,448
Yes. Some are supplied to the military,

991
00:59:56,531 --> 00:59:58,116
others are used to monitor wildfires,

992
00:59:58,199 --> 01:00:00,368
and one was in the air just for testing,

993
01:00:00,452 --> 01:00:02,370
so I moved that one to Seongwon's studio.

994
01:00:03,330 --> 01:00:04,331
Oh!

995
01:00:06,750 --> 01:00:08,418
[Isoo] Four, three,

996
01:00:09,169 --> 01:00:10,211
five, three, zero.

997
01:00:11,546 --> 01:00:13,006
-[in English] Connect.
-[digital beeping]

998
01:00:16,801 --> 01:00:18,261
[in Korean] It's live.

999
01:00:18,345 --> 01:00:19,512
This should do, right?

1000
01:00:19,596 --> 01:00:21,222
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

1001
01:00:22,432 --> 01:00:23,433
Whoa.

1002
01:00:23,516 --> 01:00:25,769
I've never seen
such a cool chaebol before.

1003
01:00:25,852 --> 01:00:27,103
You're so cool, Detective Jin.

1004
01:00:27,187 --> 01:00:29,064
You've never seen a chaebol before?

1005
01:00:29,147 --> 01:00:30,148
It's no big deal.

1006
01:00:30,231 --> 01:00:32,609
Uh-uh. No, Jin Isoo.

1007
01:00:32,692 --> 01:00:34,152
You're impressive.

1008
01:00:34,235 --> 01:00:35,362
[all chuckling]

1009
01:00:35,445 --> 01:00:37,364
Really? This is nothing.

1010
01:00:37,447 --> 01:00:38,615
Honestly.

1011
01:00:40,700 --> 01:00:41,826
-[Minjae sighs]
-[♪ music fades]

1012
01:00:42,744 --> 01:00:44,996
If I was going to work
with someone like you,

1013
01:00:45,080 --> 01:00:46,957
I seriously wouldn't have quit.

1014
01:00:47,582 --> 01:00:50,251
How can you say that
when you quit after working with me?

1015
01:00:50,335 --> 01:00:52,545
Well, it's true.

1016
01:00:52,629 --> 01:00:53,880
Is there anything you can't do?

1017
01:00:54,631 --> 01:00:57,008
Not much, really. Mmm.

1018
01:00:57,092 --> 01:00:58,176
[chuckles]

1019
01:00:58,259 --> 01:01:02,263
This is a guy who buys an entire house
just because he wants to see the basement.

1020
01:01:02,347 --> 01:01:03,723
[♪ soft piano music playing in background]

1021
01:01:03,807 --> 01:01:05,433
[exhales incredulously] That's crazy.

1022
01:01:06,101 --> 01:01:09,270
Hyera, doesn't that give you
a huge dopamine rush?

1023
01:01:09,354 --> 01:01:12,691
-Is your brain okay?
-Every day is a roller coaster. Mmm.

1024
01:01:12,774 --> 01:01:14,526
The car we were driving blows up,

1025
01:01:14,609 --> 01:01:16,528
twin magicians show up.

1026
01:01:16,611 --> 01:01:19,406
That sounds so much fun. I'm jealous.

1027
01:01:20,240 --> 01:01:22,325
Join us. Come work for me.

1028
01:01:23,868 --> 01:01:25,286
Should I try joining the force again?

1029
01:01:25,370 --> 01:01:26,454
[chuckles]

1030
01:01:28,331 --> 01:01:30,667
-Hey, where are you going?
-The restroom.

1031
01:01:35,213 --> 01:01:36,548
[door opens]

1032
01:01:36,631 --> 01:01:38,049
-[sighs deeply]
-[door closes]

1033
01:01:39,551 --> 01:01:40,552
[Minjae] Thank you.

1034
01:01:41,845 --> 01:01:43,555
Kim Heejun's death

1035
01:01:44,389 --> 01:01:45,974
was a weight on her conscience.

1036
01:01:47,100 --> 01:01:48,101
And for me, too.

1037
01:01:48,184 --> 01:01:50,020
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

1038
01:01:51,062 --> 01:01:53,481
Couldn't we have prevented it?

1039
01:01:54,941 --> 01:01:56,609
Was it maybe our fault?

1040
01:01:59,738 --> 01:02:01,573
I ran away from that like a coward,

1041
01:02:03,241 --> 01:02:04,701
while Hyera just endured it.

1042
01:02:06,828 --> 01:02:09,372
Saving Areum means a lot to us.

1043
01:02:14,085 --> 01:02:18,256
If it's with you, I think
we'll be able to catch Yu Seongwon.

1044
01:02:19,466 --> 01:02:20,842
Of course, we can, huh.

1045
01:02:21,342 --> 01:02:22,844
We'll catch that bastard

1046
01:02:23,470 --> 01:02:26,181
and isolate him from society for good.

1047
01:02:26,264 --> 01:02:27,557
-Cheers.
-[Minjae] Cheers.

1048
01:02:27,640 --> 01:02:28,933
-[Hyera] Hey, me too.
-[door closes]

1049
01:02:30,060 --> 01:02:31,102
[chuckles softly]

1050
01:02:31,770 --> 01:02:33,772
All right, let's do this.

1051
01:02:33,855 --> 01:02:35,065
-Let's do this!
-Let's do this!

1052
01:02:38,777 --> 01:02:39,819
[♪ music fades]

1053
01:02:49,662 --> 01:02:50,705
[groans]

1054
01:02:50,789 --> 01:02:52,540
God, my head. [sighs]

1055
01:02:56,377 --> 01:02:58,963
[sighs] I must be out of my mind.

1056
01:03:01,007 --> 01:03:02,092
[sighs wearily]

1057
01:03:03,593 --> 01:03:05,720
[chuckles] Roller coaster.

1058
01:03:08,348 --> 01:03:10,475
[grunts, groans]

1059
01:03:12,268 --> 01:03:14,145
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

1060
01:03:17,690 --> 01:03:19,067
[♪ music swells]

1061
01:03:22,362 --> 01:03:23,404
What's all this?

1062
01:03:23,488 --> 01:03:25,073
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

1063
01:03:44,759 --> 01:03:46,177
[♪ music turns ominous]

1064
01:03:50,598 --> 01:03:52,350
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

1065
01:03:55,436 --> 01:03:56,729
[Younghwan laughing] Huh?

1066
01:03:56,813 --> 01:03:58,439
<i>My friend, Jin Isoo. </i>[laughs]

1067
01:04:00,567 --> 01:04:01,609
[Isoo] <i>Younghwan, you, again!</i>

1068
01:04:02,318 --> 01:04:03,319
You want to try, too?

1069
01:04:03,403 --> 01:04:05,321
No! Please... Don't!

1070
01:04:05,405 --> 01:04:08,366
I told you I'd never see you
if you did it again.

1071
01:04:14,789 --> 01:04:17,125
<i>You should undergo</i>
<i>a proper investigation and quit drugs.</i>

1072
01:04:17,208 --> 01:04:20,587
All my life,
I've never thought of you as a friend.

1073
01:04:23,047 --> 01:04:24,632
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1074
01:04:28,344 --> 01:04:29,387
Jin Isoo.

1075
01:04:32,974 --> 01:04:34,184
[♪ music swells]

1076
01:04:47,405 --> 01:04:48,406
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 10

1077
01:04:48,489 --> 01:04:49,908
A BLOOD TRAIL SURROUNDS JIN ISOO

1078
01:04:49,991 --> 01:04:52,160
[♪ mellow emotional music playing]

1079
01:05:14,515 --> 01:05:17,936
Special Cast. Jeon Hyebin

1080
01:05:25,902 --> 01:05:26,903
What happened?

1081
01:05:26,986 --> 01:05:28,488
[Junyoung] He's Isoo's
middle school classmate.

1082
01:05:28,571 --> 01:05:30,281
Get a grip.
You have to remember something!

1083
01:05:30,365 --> 01:05:33,243
[detective] <i>Jin Isoo, you're under arrest</i>
<i>for the murder of Kim Younghwan.</i>

1084
01:05:33,326 --> 01:05:34,786
-You two fought, didn't you?
-Yes.

1085
01:05:34,869 --> 01:05:36,287
[Younghwan] <i>Your friend</i>
<i>came to see you, punk.</i>

1086
01:05:36,371 --> 01:05:37,372
You're finished.

1087
01:05:37,455 --> 01:05:38,665
I heard someone reported me.

1088
01:05:38,748 --> 01:05:40,416
[Isoo, over recording] <i>I killed someone.</i>

1089
01:05:40,500 --> 01:05:41,542
Got nothing left to deny?

1090
01:05:41,626 --> 01:05:43,086
[Hyera] <i>They went in with a set narrative.</i>

1091
01:05:43,169 --> 01:05:44,712
We're from Internal Affairs.

1092
01:05:44,796 --> 01:05:46,589
They found a high dose
of drugs in his system.

1093
01:05:46,673 --> 01:05:49,175
Does taking that drug
for the first time make you violent?

1094
01:05:49,259 --> 01:05:51,511
People with a lot
of pent-up anger tend to snap.

1095
01:05:51,594 --> 01:05:52,929
[Seongwon] <i>Jin Isoo could be the killer.</i>

1096
01:05:53,012 --> 01:05:55,515
Isoo! Maybe you've been holding it all in.

1097
01:05:55,598 --> 01:05:57,558
<i>And it just blew up on Younghwan.</i>

1098
01:05:58,518 --> 01:06:00,228
-[bang]
-Once you admit it,

1099
01:06:00,311 --> 01:06:01,813
you will be free.

1100
01:06:01,896 --> 01:06:02,981
[♪ song fades]

1101
01:06:04,857 --> 01:06:06,526
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

1102
01:06:14,033 --> 01:06:15,243
[Younghwan] <i>Jin Isoo.</i>

1103
01:06:15,326 --> 01:06:16,452
<i>Goodbye.</i>

1104
01:06:18,788 --> 01:06:20,623
[Younghwan laughing maniacally]

1105
01:06:37,682 --> 01:06:38,766
[squelch]

1106
01:06:38,850 --> 01:06:40,018
[♪ music swells]

1107
01:06:44,689 --> 01:06:45,940
[♪ music fades]

1108
01:06:46,024 --> 01:06:48,026
Translated by Hyesoo Lee

